infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Charges billed per outcome: no key vs idempotency key
  desc Same retries, two designs — duplicate side effects vs an exactly-once replay
  compares
    - label Without idempotency key — charges grow with each retry
      children
        - label Response delivered: 1 charge
          desc Happy path — the side effect fires exactly once
        - label Lost, client retries once: 2 charges
          desc The server can't tell the retry apart, so it charges again
        - label Lost, client retries 3 times: 4 charges
          desc Every duplicate POST re-runs the side effect
    - label With idempotency key — always 1 charge
      children
        - label Response delivered: 1 charge
          desc Same happy path, key recorded with the result
        - label Lost, client retries once: 1 charge (replay)
          desc Server matches the key and replays the stored response
        - label Lost, client retries 3 times: 1 charge (replay)
          desc Same key every retry — no business logic re-runs
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
